The site states that the icons are original and free to use under the MIT licence.
`get_set` returns set id, label, and icon names. It does not return a separate upstream license.
The licence page also says a few hand icons follow shapes from Phosphor (MIT), Tabler (MIT), and Lucide (ISC). Those licences apply to those shapes.

The shell adds the sidebar, the chat toggle, and the solid variants a selected row uses. Solid is the selected state only.

